what's going on guys today i'm going to  be giving my honest thoughts on jiu  jitsu kaizen after finally catching up  with the manga  like a lot of you who are likely  watching this video i watched season one  as it was airing but i didn't really  feel the immediate need to start reading  the series  eventually i did get around to it and  the expectations i had going in were  blown away  as there were a ton of surprising twists  and just hard-hitting scenes  that make jiu-jitsu kaizen super  interesting in this video i'm going to  explain the elements of this series i  like and dislike without giving away any  spoilers  and hopefully after that you'll be more  inclined to read it yourself if you  haven't already  as usual don't forget to hit that sub  button and drop a like if you think i  should do more jiu-jitsu kaizen content  in the future  okay so the first thing i loved with the  characters themselves considering anyone  who's really relevant has a unique  personality  coupled with clear motivations that make  sense mkamara in particular was a great  side character  and the way things unfolded in regards  to him was probably one of my favorite  parts of the series  gojo's cockiness and general demeanor is  another highlight but the manga changed  how i perceived his importance  from season one you do understand that  he is the strongest sorcerer but the  manga just makes it clear how  rare his ability is and how he's  basically a once in a lifetime  phenomenon that basically holds  everything together  that's why his dream to reset jiu  jitsu's society makes perfect sense  since he wants to foster strong allies  who can one day fill the void and make  it so he's not holding everything on his  back  there are other characters like gojo who  have a similar threatening aura  in that whenever they're involved you  feel confident they're gonna win or at  least do serious damage to whoever  they're fighting  examples include yuta mojito tsukuna  obviously  all those guys have serious main  character energy and is usually an  entertaining time whenever they're  involved  sukuna in particular is really  intriguing to me because he very  obviously has an elaborate plan in place  going all the way back to when he made  that binding vow with yuji  yet even now it's still hard to piece  together what he's planning  there are a ton of other characters who  i think are great including chozo megumi  toto i mean there's just too many  and surprisingly you know chozo was one  who i didn't expect to like but as the  series progressed i did enjoy whenever i  saw him more and more  next up another good thing was how my  expectations were constantly being  subverted in a way that felt natural  normally when you reach a certain part  in a storyline you have a rough idea of  how things might go but akutami  frequently diverts from the  reasonable part as you might expect  there are also times when something  crazy looks like it's about to go down  and you think to yourself they're not  really gonna do this are they  and then no they actually do follow  through with it the power system is also  pretty great  and as we all know the best ability this  series has to offer is the variety of  domain expansions  this is something that many of the best  sorceress can't even use which makes it  all the more special when someone does  actually go and do it  because the person who creates the  domain is guaranteed to land a hit  one of the aspects of the manga i liked  was the different ways people tried to  survive this impossible situation  naturally gojo survived by simply  expanding his own domain but most people  don't exactly have that option so it was  interesting seeing the other techniques  to get around this  and also the crazy scene that happened  uh with a certain member  of the xenon family the power system  also ties into politics  given that certain cursing needs can  only be used by specific families  my opinion now is that the value placed  on certain techniques is actually  fascinating  because it means the power dynamics of  the big families can change with the  flip of a coin  people like narutoshi are the best  example of this as they're thought into  positions of power even when normally  they wouldn't be asked to do so  when we look at megumi specifically he  obviously has the best or most  valuable technique of the xenon family  and in recent chapters we saw how it can  be used to his political advantage  now the topic of death is something that  jujitsu kaizen deals with incredibly  well  as it's something you actually fear in  this series when it comes to the other  manga that i read on a weekly  basis once in a while a side character  might actually die but the characters we  actually like  are nearly always guaranteed to survive  jiu jitsu kaizen subverts that  expectation in a big way  as outside of gojo yuji and magumi i  genuinely think anyone else could be  killed at any moment  when we look back at jumbo for example  he was being set up like a major  character going forward  i mean in terms of importance i would  compare him to the caliber of someone  like todoroki when he first appeared in  my academia  someone like that doesn't just get  killed off and never seen again which is  why i was half expecting jumped to  return in some way  i didn't know how it was gonna happen i  didn't know when it was gonna happen but  i was fully expecting it for a long time  and uh yeah eventually i just came to  realize this is what this series is like  like people will really just die  in the manga there were further  casualties that are even more shocking  than this one  and what it means is that the big  battles have a lot of suspense  besides the three characters i mentioned  and obviously sukuna because he's you  know in yuji's body  um besides those guys i don't think  anyone is off the table when it comes to  being killed  last thing to mention that i liked is  the element of mystery including yuji's  heritage  and potential traces at jiu jitsu high i  wouldn't say these mysteries presented  are anything too radical  but it's definitely enough to keep you  invested the thing i'm most eager to  find out about is what sukuna wants with  megumi but i'm sure we'll find out once  his plan comes together  moving on to what i didn't like about  the series number one was that sometimes  the explanation for things was  unnecessarily complicated  whether it be specific curse techniques  or a certain event that happens after  the shibuya arc  i imagine there were just much easier  ways to convey the same point  number two although it is the minority  for certain fights it was hard to  decipher what was happening from panel  to panel  however i imagine the anime will  obviously make this a lot clearer  most of the time you can tell exactly  what's going on but yeah occasionally  you'll get panels where you have to like  study what's happening just to see if  you can decipher it and even then you  might not realize what it is  final point was that the relationship  between meimei and her brother was  something that was quite strange to me i  mean it's not the first time i've seen  something like this  but there was just one scene in  particular that took it too far in my  opinion  anyway guys those are my overall spoiler  free thoughts on jujitsu kaizen  let me know in the comments what you  think of this series and drop a like as  well as i do really appreciate it  until the next one peace out
 

